# Line endings, settled once.
#
# This project grew up with both: on 2026-11-04 it had 41 CRLF files against the rest,
# because each author and each tool wrote whatever it wrote. Nothing was broken by it,
# but the first commit would otherwise record that mess for ever, and every later diff
# would be full of lines that only changed their endings.
#
# So: text is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF. Python, Qt and
# every editor on Windows read LF without complaint. The exceptions below are the files
# where Windows itself still wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which is the one thing here that still prefers CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mkv binary
*.wav binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
